questions.question:
a) Design a purlin for a trussed roof from the following data using steel rolled section with $f_y = 250\text{ MPa}$. [8]
span of roof = $10\text{m}$;
truss spacing = $4.0\text{m}$;
spacing of purlins along the slope = $2.6\text{m}$;
slope of the roof = $20^\circ$;
wind load on roof surface = $800\text{ N/m}^2$;
vertical load (dead + live) = $600\text{ N/m}^2$.

b) Teak wood floor beams are used at spacing of $3\text{m}$ centres. The span of the beam is $5\text{m}$. The dead load of span is $3\text{ KN/m}^2$ and live load $2\text{ KN/m}^2$. Design the beam if end bearings are $25\text{cm}$ at both ends. Assume necessary data if required.

